# What npm leaves out of the package. When this file exists npm stops reading
# .gitignore, so it carries every .gitignore rule except ONE: git-sha.json.
# That stamp (scripts/stamp-git-sha.mjs, written at prepack) is untracked in git
# on purpose and exists to be SHIPPED — it is how an npm-installed copy, which has
# no .git, reports the commit it was built from. With .gitignore as the only
# ignore file it was silently excluded from every tarball.
# tests/npm-ignore-parity.test.mjs keeps the two files in step.

